"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision 2026-09-06: HARD CONSTRAINT — all sessions share one GitHub/Gerrit/Jira credential; submit serialization REJECTED (unacceptable friction for parallel development). Any design must make ownership visible without serializing; re-escalate if a decision is still needed.","timestamp":1788761531816878001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Ownership-visibility archaeology (2026-09-06): Gerrit offers useful metadata but not true per-session ownership under one account. Native surfaces found: topics (`PUT /changes/{id}/topic`), hashtags (`POST /changes/{id}/hashtags`), ReviewInput `tag` on change messages/reviews, attention set (user/account oriented, weak under a shared service user), and custom keyed values (`/custom_keyed_values`, documented as small external-system IDs). Repo precedent: darksome-starry-sable used Gerrit as source of truth and keyed transient markers by `change_id + patchset_SHA`; dismal-uncheerful-rockrat required fresh Verified on the exact patchset SHA before submit and used topic as `stack_id`. CONTRIBUTING.md and ADR 0047 record the current Rebase-If-Necessary + plain Submit model.\n\nSubmit-safety finding: Gerrit REST supports the exact CAS shape we need. `GET /changes/{id}/revisions/current` returns RevisionInfo including the current commit SHA/ref. More importantly, `POST /changes/{id}/revisions/{revision-id}/submit` submits a specific revision and returns 409 Conflict if that revision is not current (“revision ... is not current revision”). That is a native submit-if-current precondition; no global serialization required.\n\nRecommended design: on push/comment, stamp session identity as a hashtag or custom keyed value (e.g. `rebar-session=<session-id>`; hashtag if UI visibility matters, custom keyed value if machine-readability matters), and before submit always re-read current revision + live labels, then call revision-scoped submit on the SHA whose votes were inspected. If the current SHA differs or revision-submit returns 409, refuse loudly: another session changed/rebased it. Verdict: resolved-with-evidence / recommended design; needs user sign-off only for the metadata vehicle (hashtag vs custom keyed value vs both), not for the safety guard.","timestamp":1788763495531926001}],"created_at":1788575886262396001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4560ee53-cd82-4c5d-ab3d-0686733556f5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5202-3ac4-fe07-454a"},{"link_uuid":"802c34d5-c719-4b00-92e8-76fab781b691","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2ae6-cae4-4c1a-472f"},{"link_uuid":"53700132-3c24-4516-b5f5-d2b48e8809c1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4d79-8cca-b81e-4821"},{"link_uuid":"8180f9bb-d1d3-4a0e-94e9-0a98f09b2c5a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0cbd-1502-bebc-4e08"},{"link_uuid":"a902d56b-c529-4833-be86-07e728550e74","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d4cc-7c53-b286-4eeb"}],"description":"## The hazard\n\nEvery concurrent Claude/agent session on this host pushes, amends and submits Gerrit changes under\nthe SAME `RebarBotNava` identity. Gerrit therefore reports `owner:self` for changes belonging to\nother sessions, and there is no field anywhere in the change that says which session is driving it.\nOwnership is invisible at exactly the moment it matters: when deciding whether to amend or submit.\n\n## Two instances, both on 2026-09-04/05\n\n**(1) A submit raced a live rebase by 39 seconds.** An orchestrator saw change 2645 at\n`LLM-Review +1` / `Verified +1` and attempted to submit it. Gerrit refused with `HTTP 409` (rebase\nconflict on `docs/env-vars.md`), so the orchestrator dispatched an agent to rebase and re-push.\nThat agent's first act was to check for a concurrent owner, and found:\n\n- patch set 4 had been uploaded **39 seconds earlier** (02:35:39 UTC; the check ran at 02:36:18);\n- `current_revision` was already `10af5f28bcaf`, not the `56787a044821` the submit had failed on;\n- a worktree at `/Users/joeoakhart/reb-640-terraform-grounding` held `10af5f28bcaf` with a reflog\n  showing `rebase (start)` -> `rebase (continue)` -> `rebase (finish)` — another session had\n  resolved the identical conflict minutes before.\n\nHad the agent proceeded it would have pushed a competing patch set 5 over 39-second-old work. It\nwas stopped only because the dispatch brief happened to include an ownership check. Nothing in the\nsystem would have prevented it.\n\n**(2) A subagent misattributed a merge to a third party.** Earlier the same night a subagent\nreported that change 2642 \"merged without it submitting\", treating it as an anomaly worth\ninvestigating. The submitter was its own orchestrator. The subagent could not tell, because both\nact as `RebarBotNava`.\n\n## Why it is worth fixing rather than working around\n\nThe two failure directions are asymmetric and both bad. Case (1) is a WRITE race that silently\ndiscards another session's work; case (2) is wasted investigation into a phantom. Neither is\ndetectable after the fact from the change itself.\n\nIt also interacts badly with the vote model: an upload marks prior votes **Outdated**, so a\ncompeting patch set does not merely duplicate effort — it RESETS two gates that had already passed,\nreturning the change to the back of a saturated CI queue. In case (1) that is exactly what\nhappened: 2645's `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` from PS3 are both listed as Outdated on PS4, so\na change that was submittable now has zero live votes.\n\n## Directions (none endorsed; the ticket is the problem statement)\n\n- Per-session Gerrit identities, so `owner` is meaningful. Highest fidelity, largest credential and\n  access-control cost; note `RebarBotNava`'s Contributor rights would need replicating per identity.\n- A machine-local claim registry mapping change number -> worktree/session, written on push and\n  read before amend/submit. Cheap, but advisory only, and another session can ignore it.\n- Make the check mandatory rather than remembered: document (and script) the pre-submit\n  verification the agent above performed by luck of its brief — confirm `current_revision` matches\n  what you inspected, confirm votes are live rather than Outdated, and check `git worktree list`\n  for a local holder before amending someone else's change.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] The ownership question is answerable BEFORE an amend or submit, by a documented and scripted\n      check rather than by an agent happening to think of it.\n- [x] A submit is refused, or at minimum loudly warned, when the `current_revision` differs from\n      the revision whose votes were inspected. Proven by attempting a submit against a\n      deliberately stale revision and observing the refusal.\n- [x] The interaction with vote invalidation is stated wherever the push flow is documented: an\n      unnecessary patch set RESETS `LLM-Review` and `Verified` to Outdated and re-queues the\n      change, so re-pushing a green change is destructive, not neutral.\n- [x] Whichever direction is chosen is recorded with its reasoning, including an explicit decision\n      on per-session identities (adopt or reject with a reason) rather than defaulting to the\n      cheapest option by omission.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py","reason":"add Gerrit-native session hashtag and revision-scoped submit helper methods"},{"path":"scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py","reason":"documented helper for revision-scoped safe submit using git credential helper and session hashtag"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gerrit_submit_if_current_8b1c.py","reason":"regression coverage for revision-scoped submit and session hashtag endpoints"},{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"agent workflow guidance for session hashtags and revision-scoped submit"},{"path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","reason":"human workflow guidance for session hashtags and revision-scoped submit"},{"path":"docs/releasing.md","reason":"release submit guidance uses revision-scoped helper"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0cbd-1502-bebc-4e08"],["relates_to","2ae6-cae4-4c1a-472f"],["relates_to","4d79-8cca-b81e-4821"],["relates_to","5202-3ac4-fe07-454a"],["relates_to","d4cc-7c53-b286-4eeb"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"0d9e1791-a418-4b3b-9866-3c52dff62f7d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8b1c-c577-366b-47d5","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Concurrent sessions share one RebarBotNava Gerrit identity, so change ownership is invisible: a submit raced another session's rebase by 39 seconds and would have reset two passing gates","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["042b32d6-8f94-4877-a0d7-0bf24e1ad200","3b56a59b-8807-4ffd-8c9b-d8c0d824e52b","0308ebf6-c9da-4512-b8b2-ee9de509a00f","0d9e1791-a418-4b3b-9866-3c52dff62f7d","e0a19bee-a947-40a7-bf20-02c9eb3cd3b1","e597bfda-4f6f-406b-98d0-7b5d5bf353f8","4560ee53-cd82-4c5d-ab3d-0686733556f5","802c34d5-c719-4b00-92e8-76fab781b691","53700132-3c24-4516-b5f5-d2b48e8809c1","8180f9bb-d1d3-4a0e-94e9-0a98f09b2c5a","bbf51bb4-ea9d-4d50-a419-6aa161fa40b6","1278e95d-264d-47ad-b340-4720de8f0664","a902d56b-c529-4833-be86-07e728550e74"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788792286469369026,"uuid":"b7b55289-f812-4424-8e47-b366995f6ce9"}